            <div xml:id="d279">

                <pb facs="0439" n="359" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg359"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.20/1132: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dodd</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-10-12T17:00:00+01:00">October 12, 1936—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 12—12:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>301. Embassy’s telegram 294, September 28, 6 p.m. The military action outlined
                    went into effect on October 11th according to the Military Attaché but will not
                    be publicly announced.</p>
                <p>Copies to London, Rome, Paris.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dodd</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
